{
  "public": {
    "id": "range-sum-updates",
    "slug": "range-sum-updates",
    "version": "1.0.0",
    "title": "Range Sums with Point Updates",
    "description": "Maintain a fresh numeric array for each call. Process operations in order: [\"set\", index, value] replaces the value at the zero-based index and produces null; [\"sum\", left, right] produces the sum from left through right, including both endpoints. Return one result per operation, in the same order; there is no constructor operation. values contains 1 to 800 integers, and operations contains 0 to 500 operations. Every initial or assigned value is between -1000000 and 1000000. Indices are valid integers, and each sum has left no greater than right. All operations have exactly three entries and are either set or sum. Repeated sets replace rather than add; reads observe all preceding sets. Aim for logarithmic time per operation using a Fenwick tree or segment tree.",
    "difficulty": "medium",
    "concepts": ["arrays", "fenwick-tree", "prefix-sums"],
    "hints": [
      "A prefix sum query can produce an inclusive range sum by subtracting two prefixes.",
      "Store the current values so an assignment can be converted into a delta for the tree."
    ],
    "attribution": "Original Bekor statement, examples, tests, explanation and solutions authored in 2026. Uses a standard algorithmic technique; no third-party exercise text or solution code used.",
